: Hello everyone! Welcome to WeAreDevelopers World Congress 2026, Berlin! Today I'm going to talk about gRPC-Gateway, a powerful tool that bridges two worlds - gRPC and REST.
: Let me start with a problem that I'm sure many of you have run into. You're building microservices, and internally everything talks gRPC because it's fast and strongly typed. But then your frontend team comes along and says - "we can't easily call gRPC from the browser, we need REST and JSON." Or your mobile team, or an external partner, says the same thing. So what do most teams end up doing? They write the same API twice - once for gRPC, once for REST. And then those two implementations slowly drift apart. Bugs creep in. New fields get added to one but not the other.
: That's exactly the problem gRPC-Gateway solves. It lets you write your API code just once, in a single protobuf definition, and serve it to both gRPC clients and RESTful HTTP clients at the same time.
: This is a real game-changer for modern microservices architectures because you get the best of both worlds - the performance and type-safety of gRPC for internal calls, and the universal compatibility of REST for external clients - without writing duplicate code.
: Over the next 30 minutes I'll walk you through what gRPC-Gateway is, the different ways you can map HTTP routes to gRPC methods, build a full hello world service live in the slides, and finally cover the advanced features that make this production-ready - custom URL mappings, streaming, and error handling.

